## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose cross-region telemetry issues in a service mesh with TLS, tenancy boundaries, and UDP paths.

## Key Concepts
- Edge load balancers TLS session resumption; per-tenant sidecar resource usage; MTU discovery and path fragmentation;
- NAT64 state handling; cross-region tunnel dynamics; observability across L4-L7 boundaries.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: quick script outline to surface TLS ticket counts from edge LB logs
const fs = require('fs');
const logs = fs.readFileSync('/var/log/edge/tls.log','utf8');
const tickets = logs.match(/TLS_ticket:(\d+)/g) || [];
console.log('Tickets seen:', tickets.length);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely roll out TLS ticket lifetime changes across regions?
- Which metrics differentiate sidecar starvation from path MTU fragmentation in this scenario?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical DNS troubleshooting skills, anycast path reasoning, and ability to design a reproducible diagnostic plan with concrete commands.

## Key Concepts

- DNS resolution and TTL behavior
- Anycast routing and cache effects
- Health checks and traffic steering
- Reproducibility and data collection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: parse a dns trace to extract served A record
function extractRegion(traceLines) {
  const line = traceLines.find(l => l.includes('A')) || traceLines[0];
  const match = line.match(/([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}/);
  return match ? match[0] : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate a rollback plan if regional DNS changes cause regression?
- Which metrics signal a successful stabilization?
